# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduce the effects of noise and errors {#reduce-the-effects-of-noise-and-errors}"
msgstr "Kurangkan kesan hingar dan ralat {#reduce-the-effects-of-noise-and-errors}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Several Qiskit addons focus specifically on reducing the impact of noise and hardware imperfections.\n"
msgstr "Beberapa addon Qiskit memberi tumpuan khusus kepada mengurangkan kesan hingar dan ketidaksempurnaan perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation and noise-aware circuit transformations {#operator-backpropagation-and-noise-aware-circuit-transformations}"
msgstr "Operator backpropagation dan transformasi litar sedar-hingar {#operator-backpropagation-and-noise-aware-circuit-transformations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have already discussed operator propagation in the context of coherent Pauli checks in error correction. However, operator propagation is useful more generally. There are two main ways to use the propagation of an operator through a quantum circuit: (1) absorb the last few layers of a quantum circuit into the observables being measured, and (2) take into account the likely effects of errors in the circuit, and compensate for them by measuring a different observable. The next two tools use these approaches.\n"
msgstr "Kita telah membincangkan perambatan pengendali dalam konteks semakan Pauli koheren dalam pembetulan ralat. Namun, perambatan pengendali berguna secara lebih umum. Terdapat dua cara utama untuk menggunakan perambatan pengendali melalui litar kuantum: (1) menyerap beberapa lapisan terakhir litar kuantum ke dalam observable yang diukur, dan (2) mengambil kira kesan ralat yang mungkin dalam litar, dan mengimbanginya dengan mengukur observable yang berbeza. Dua alat seterusnya menggunakan pendekatan ini.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"
msgstr "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Operator backpropagation](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp) reduces circuit depth by absorbing gates from the end of a circuit into the measured observable. For example, consider the following circuit.\n"
msgstr "[Operator backpropagation](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp) mengurangkan kedalaman litar dengan menyerap gate dari hujung litar ke dalam observable yang diukur. Sebagai contoh, pertimbangkan litar berikut.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing a quantum circuit with several entangling and rotation layers, followed by a ladder of CNOTs from qubit 0 down to qubit 5. Finally, a Z measurement is made on qubit 5.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/backprop.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing a quantum circuit with several entangling and rotation layers, followed by a ladder of CNOTs from qubit 0 down to qubit 5. Finally, a Z measurement is made on qubit 5.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/backprop.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This circuit contains rotation and entangling layers that appear nontrivial, followed by a ladder of CNOT gates and a measurement of `Z` on qubit 5. This circuit has a two-qubit depth of 7. This depth is before transpilation. In practice, you typically apply backpropagation after transpilation, but this example is for teaching purposes only. Recall that there are rules for propagating an observable past a gate. In particular, when a CNOT gate has target $q_t$ and control $q_c$, a $Z_t$ observable on $q_t$ becomes $Z_c Z_t$ when propagated backward past the CNOT gate: $Z_t \\rightarrow Z_c Z_t$. In this example circuit, if you propagate the observable $Z_5$ back through the entire ladder of CNOT gates, you get the observable $Z_5 Z_4 Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$, or in standard Qiskit notation, simply $ZZZZZZ$. If we measure this observable instead of only $Z_5$, we can remove the entire ladder of CNOT gates, which reduces the two-qubit depth from 7 to 2. This observable still requires a measurement in only one basis on each qubit, so it does not increase the number of shots that we require. This is not always the case. Generally, more complicated observables require more shots, and sometimes more measurements in different bases.\n"
msgstr "Litar ini mengandungi lapisan putaran dan lapisan berpaut yang kelihatan tidak remeh, diikuti tangga gate CNOT dan pengukuran `Z` pada qubit 5. Litar ini mempunyai kedalaman dua-qubit 7. Kedalaman ini adalah sebelum transpilation. Dalam praktik, anda biasanya menggunakan backpropagation selepas transpilation, tetapi contoh ini hanya untuk tujuan pengajaran. Ingat bahawa terdapat peraturan untuk merambatkan observable melepasi sesuatu gate. Khususnya, apabila gate CNOT mempunyai sasaran $q_t$ dan kawalan $q_c$, observable $Z_t$ pada $q_t$ menjadi $Z_c Z_t$ apabila dirambatkan ke belakang melepasi gate CNOT: $Z_t \\rightarrow Z_c Z_t$. Dalam litar contoh ini, jika anda merambatkan observable $Z_5$ ke belakang melalui keseluruhan tangga gate CNOT, anda mendapat observable $Z_5 Z_4 Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$, atau dalam tatatanda Qiskit piawai, ringkasnya $ZZZZZZ$. Jika kita mengukur observable ini dan bukannya hanya $Z_5$, kita boleh membuang keseluruhan tangga gate CNOT, yang mengurangkan kedalaman dua-qubit daripada 7 kepada 2. Observable ini masih memerlukan pengukuran dalam satu asas sahaja pada setiap qubit, jadi ia tidak meningkatkan bilangan shot yang kita perlukan. Ini tidak selalu berlaku. Secara amnya, observable yang lebih kompleks memerlukan lebih banyak shot, dan kadangkala lebih banyak pengukuran dalam asas yang berbeza.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The overall strategy of operator backpropagation includes the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Strategi keseluruhan operator backpropagation merangkumi langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shorten the executed circuit\n"
msgstr "Memendekkan litar yang dilaksanakan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replace the original observable with an expanded observable\n"
msgstr "Menggantikan observable asal dengan observable yang diperluas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trade circuit depth for increased sampling requirements\n"
msgstr "Menukar kedalaman litar dengan keperluan pensampelan yang meningkat\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous circuit is an obvious example in which backpropagation is advantageous. In general, however, it is not easy to identify the circuits that benefit most from backpropagation. To decide when to use backpropagation, check how much depth you can remove from your circuit, and weigh that reduction against the increased sampling requirements.\n"
msgstr "Litar sebelumnya ialah contoh jelas di mana backpropagation memberi kelebihan. Secara amnya, bagaimanapun, tidak mudah untuk mengenal pasti litar yang paling mendapat manfaat daripada backpropagation. Untuk memutuskan bila hendak menggunakan backpropagation, semak berapa banyak kedalaman yang boleh anda buang daripada litar anda, dan timbang pengurangan itu berbanding keperluan pensampelan yang meningkat.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagated noise absorption (PNA) {#propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"
msgstr "Propagated noise absorption (PNA) {#propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Propagated noise absorption](/addons/qiskit-addon-pna) is structurally similar to operator backpropagation. However, instead of propagating an operator back through the ideal gates in a circuit, PNA incorporates a learned noise model and propagates the effects of noise directly into the observable. PNA does the following:\n"
msgstr "[Propagated noise absorption](/addons/qiskit-addon-pna) secara struktur serupa dengan operator backpropagation. Namun, daripada merambatkan pengendali ke belakang melalui gate ideal dalam litar, PNA menggabungkan model hingar yang dipelajari dan merambatkan kesan hingar terus ke dalam observable. PNA melakukan perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learns noise behavior from the hardware\n"
msgstr "Mempelajari tingkah laku hingar daripada perkakasan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagates the noise model through the circuit\n"
msgstr "Merambatkan model hingar melalui litar\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Produces a modified observable that compensates for gate noise\n"
msgstr "Menghasilkan observable terubah suai yang mengimbangi hingar gate\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing the gate errors on many layers of a quantum circuit being propagated forward to the final observable measurement.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/pna.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing the gate errors on many layers of a quantum circuit being propagated forward to the final observable measurement.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/pna.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the modified observable is measured on noisy hardware, the resulting expectation values better approximate the ideal noiseless result. PNA has two types of overhead. First, you must learn the noise model, which requires running additional circuits. Second, PNA can produce more complicated observables, which can increase sampling requirements.\n"
msgstr "Apabila observable terubah suai diukur pada perkakasan berhingar, nilai jangkaan yang terhasil menghampiri keputusan ideal tanpa hingar dengan lebih baik. PNA mempunyai dua jenis overhed. Pertama, anda mesti mempelajari model hingar, yang memerlukan menjalankan litar tambahan. Kedua, PNA boleh menghasilkan observable yang lebih kompleks, yang boleh meningkatkan keperluan pensampelan.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit cutting {#circuit-cutting}"
msgstr "Circuit cutting {#circuit-cutting}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Circuit cutting](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-cutting) partitions a large circuit into smaller subcircuits that can run independently. You then make enough measurements to recombine the results. Circuit cutting does the following:\n"
msgstr "[Circuit cutting](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-cutting) membahagikan litar besar kepada subLitar yang lebih kecil yang boleh dijalankan secara bebas. Anda kemudian membuat pengukuran yang mencukupi untuk menggabungkan semula keputusan. Circuit cutting melakukan perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduces hardware requirements\n"
msgstr "Mengurangkan keperluan perkakasan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Allows computations larger than available qubit counts (wider circuits)\n"
msgstr "Membenarkan pengiraan yang lebih besar daripada bilangan qubit yang tersedia (litar lebih lebar)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Helps address depth and connectivity limitations (deeper circuits)\n"
msgstr "Membantu menangani had kedalaman dan ketersambungan (litar lebih dalam)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconstructs the original result through classical post-processing\n"
msgstr "Membina semula keputusan asal melalui pasca-pemprosesan klasik\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing two circuits being cut, so that they can be run separately and recombined later in post-processing.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/cutting.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing two circuits being cut, so that they can be run separately and recombined later in post-processing.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/cutting.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic {#samplomatic}"
msgstr "Samplomatic {#samplomatic}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many of the techniques in the previous sections complement other suppression and mitigation methods covered throughout this course, including:\n"
msgstr "Banyak teknik dalam bahagian sebelumnya melengkapi kaedah penindasan dan pengurangan lain yang dibincangkan sepanjang kursus ini, termasuk:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling\n"
msgstr "Dynamical decoupling\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "M3\n"
msgstr "M3\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX\n"
msgstr "TREX\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE)\n"
msgstr "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)\n"
msgstr "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In many workflows, you can apply different techniques to different regions of the same circuit. As we have seen, many of these techniques also come with quantum overhead. We therefore sometimes need fine, detailed control over noise learning, sampling, and the application of twirling sequences. These are some of the motivations behind Samplomatic.\n"
msgstr "Dalam banyak aliran kerja, anda boleh menggunakan teknik berbeza pada kawasan berbeza dalam litar yang sama. Seperti yang telah kita lihat, banyak teknik ini juga disertai overhed kuantum. Oleh itu, kadangkala kita memerlukan kawalan halus dan terperinci ke atas pembelajaran hingar, pensampelan, dan penggunaan jujukan twirling. Ini antara motivasi di sebalik Samplomatic.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Samplomatic](/addons/samplomatic) is an open-source library that enables customized sampling, randomization, and error-mitigation workflows.\n"
msgstr "[Samplomatic](/addons/samplomatic) ialah pustaka sumber terbuka yang membolehkan aliran kerja pensampelan, perawakan, dan pengurangan ralat yang disesuaikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its first task is to analyze a circuit and divide it into labeled regions, or boxes. These boxes serve two purposes:\n"
msgstr "Tugas pertamanya ialah menganalisis litar dan membahagikannya kepada kawasan berlabel, atau kotak. Kotak ini mempunyai dua tujuan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "They visually partition the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ia membahagikan litar secara visual.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "They create indexed regions that can be configured independently.\n"
msgstr "Ia mencipta kawasan berindeks yang boleh dikonfigurasi secara bebas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Users can attach annotations that describe how each box should be treated during execution. Examples include:\n"
msgstr "Pengguna boleh melampirkan anotasi yang menerangkan cara setiap kotak patut dilayan semasa pelaksanaan. Contohnya termasuk:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying Pauli twirling to all boxes\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan Pauli twirling pada semua kotak\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying twirling only to selected boxes\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan twirling hanya pada kotak terpilih\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using different twirling groups in different regions\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan kumpulan twirling berbeza dalam kawasan berbeza\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Injecting learned noise into specific layers\n"
msgstr "Menyuntik hingar yang dipelajari ke dalam lapisan tertentu\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customizing mitigation strategies at a fine-grained level\n"
msgstr "Menyesuaikan strategi pengurangan pada tahap yang terperinci\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic also identifies repeated boxed regions. Because identical layers typically exhibit similar noise characteristics, you only need to perform noise learning once for each unique layer.\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic juga mengenal pasti kawasan berkotak yang berulang. Oleh kerana lapisan yang serupa biasanya menunjukkan ciri hingar yang sama, anda hanya perlu melakukan pembelajaran hingar sekali bagi setiap lapisan unik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic outputs {#samplomatic-outputs}"
msgstr "Output Samplomatic {#samplomatic-outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic produces two primary objects:\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic menghasilkan dua objek utama:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Template circuit\n"
msgstr "Litar templat\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplex\n"
msgstr "Samplex\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The template circuit is a boxed, transpiled, parameterized circuit that is ready for execution. The samplex contains all the information that is required to generate and process circuit variants. Samplex contents include:\n"
msgstr "Litar templat ialah litar berkotak, transpiled, berparameter yang sedia untuk dilaksanakan. Samplex mengandungi semua maklumat yang diperlukan untuk menjana dan memproses varian litar. Kandungan samplex termasuk:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parameter values for parameterized circuits\n"
msgstr "Nilai parameter untuk litar berparameter\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Randomization selections\n"
msgstr "Pilihan perawakan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling distributions\n"
msgstr "Taburan persampelan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing information\n"
msgstr "Maklumat pasca-pemprosesan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional execution metadata\n"
msgstr "Metadata pelaksanaan tambahan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formally, a samplex is a probability distribution over the parameters of a template circuit, together with auxiliary information that is required for execution and post-processing. An important practical advantage is that both the template circuit and the samplex are created locally on the client side. As a result, you can inspect, validate, and debug them before you use any hardware resources.\n"
msgstr "Secara formal, samplex ialah taburan kebarangkalian ke atas parameter bagi sebuah circuit templat, bersama maklumat tambahan yang diperlukan untuk pelaksanaan dan pasca-pemprosesan. Kelebihan praktikal yang penting ialah circuit templat dan samplex kedua-duanya dicipta secara setempat di sisi klien. Hasilnya, anda boleh memeriksa, mengesahkan dan menyahpepijatnya sebelum menggunakan sebarang sumber perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic has many benefits, including fine-grained control of adaptive shot allocation and randomization. It also has logistical benefits, such as structured post-processing workflows. One of the most important benefits is the reuse of learned noise information across identical layers, which can save a significant amount of quantum computing time during noise learning.\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic mempunyai banyak kelebihan, termasuk kawalan terperinci terhadap peruntukan shot adaptif dan perawakan. Ia juga mempunyai kelebihan logistik, seperti aliran kerja pasca-pemprosesan yang berstruktur. Salah satu kelebihan terpenting ialah penggunaan semula maklumat hingar yang dipelajari merentas lapisan yang serupa, yang boleh menjimatkan masa pengkomputeran kuantum dengan ketara semasa pembelajaran hingar.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones {#shaded-lightcones}"
msgstr "Shaded lightcones {#shaded-lightcones}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you decide where to apply expensive mitigation techniques, it is helpful to identify the regions of a circuit that matter most to the observable that is being measured. This need motivates the [shaded lightcones](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc) addon. The idea of a lightcone comes from relativity, in which causal relationships are constrained by the finite speed at which information can travel.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum anda memutuskan di mana hendak menggunakan teknik mitigasi yang mahal, adalah berguna untuk mengenal pasti kawasan litar yang paling penting kepada observable yang diukur. Keperluan ini mendorong addon [shaded lightcones](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc). Idea lightcone datang daripada relativiti, yang mana hubungan sebab-akibat dihadkan oleh kelajuan terhingga yang boleh dilalui maklumat.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image of spacetime. Time runs from bottom to top, and space runs from side to side. Because no causation can move through space faster than the speed of light, the region of spacetime that an event can causally influence is limited to a conical region. This is an analogy for the spreading of errors in a quantum circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image of spacetime. Time runs from bottom to top, and space runs from side to side. Because no causation can move through space faster than the speed of light, the region of spacetime that an event can causally influence is limited to a conical region. This is an analogy for the spreading of errors in a quantum circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A similar concept applies in quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr "Konsep yang serupa terpakai dalam circuit kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider a large circuit in which only a low-weight observable is of interest. A low-weight observable acts nontrivially on only a few qubits. Low-weight observables are of interest for many reasons. For example, they can represent the following:\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan circuit besar yang hanya mempunyai observable berpemberat rendah yang diminati. Observable berpemberat rendah bertindak secara tidak remeh pada hanya beberapa qubit. Observable berpemberat rendah diminati atas banyak sebab. Sebagai contoh, ia boleh mewakili perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Individual terms within a larger Hamiltonian\n"
msgstr "Sebutan individu dalam Hamiltonian yang lebih besar\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A localized interaction region\n"
msgstr "Kawasan interaksi setempat\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Information collected onto a small set of ancilla qubits\n"
msgstr "Maklumat yang dikumpulkan ke atas set kecil qubit ancilla\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other observables that involve only a few qubits\n"
msgstr "Observable lain yang melibatkan hanya beberapa qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Not every error in the circuit can affect the measurement outcome. This is especially true of Pauli errors, or any error that can be modeled as a set of Pauli operations. For example, look at the following circuit:\n"
msgstr "Tidak setiap ralat dalam circuit boleh menjejaskan hasil pengukuran. Ini terutamanya benar bagi ralat Pauli, atau sebarang ralat yang boleh dimodelkan sebagai set operasi Pauli. Sebagai contoh, lihat circuit berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit with an error on qubit 0 just before measurement. A measurement is performed only on qubit 6, and there is no entangling gate between qubits 0 and 6 in the final layer.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone-a.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit with an error on qubit 0 just before measurement. A measurement is performed only on qubit 6, and there is no entangling gate between qubits 0 and 6 in the final layer.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone-a.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Pauli error on qubit 0 in the final layer cannot influence the measurement on qubit 6, because there is no connecting gate that could propagate the error from qubit 0 to qubit 6. Note that this argument does not apply to certain non-unitary errors. For example, a T1-like transition to the ground state on qubit 0 collapses qubit 0 to a computational basis state. If qubits 0 and 6 were previously entangled (as they are in this circuit), the non-unitary error on qubit 0 can affect qubit 6. The following discussion focuses on errors that can be represented as Pauli operations, or as probabilistic mixtures of Pauli operations.\n"
msgstr "Ralat Pauli pada qubit 0 dalam lapisan terakhir tidak boleh mempengaruhi pengukuran pada qubit 6, kerana tiada gate penyambung yang boleh merambatkan ralat daripada qubit 0 ke qubit 6. Perhatikan bahawa hujah ini tidak terpakai pada ralat bukan unitari tertentu. Sebagai contoh, peralihan jenis T1 ke keadaan asas pada qubit 0 meruntuhkan qubit 0 kepada keadaan asas komputasi. Jika qubit 0 dan 6 sebelum ini terkusut (seperti dalam circuit ini), ralat bukan unitari pada qubit 0 boleh menjejaskan qubit 6. Perbincangan berikut memfokuskan pada ralat yang boleh diwakili sebagai operasi Pauli, atau sebagai campuran probabilistik operasi Pauli.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the last layer, only a Pauli error on qubit 5 or qubit 6 can directly affect the measurement on qubit 6.\n"
msgstr "Dalam lapisan terakhir, hanya ralat Pauli pada qubit 5 atau qubit 6 yang boleh menjejaskan pengukuran pada qubit 6 secara langsung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the entangling layer before that one, qubits 5 and 6 are entangled with qubits 4 and 7, respectively. Therefore, in that entangling layer or just before it, a Pauli error on any of those four qubits can affect the later measurement. You can continue to trace backward through the circuit to find the subset of gates and qubits that are causally connected to the measurement. This causal set forms a cone-shaped region in space (qubits) and time (layers), which gives rise to the term lightcone. The exact shape of the region varies from circuit to circuit. Because this analysis depends on hardware connectivity and gate placement, it is most useful after transpilation, routing, and layout optimization.\n"
msgstr "Dalam lapisan berkusut sebelum itu, qubit 5 dan 6 masing-masing terkusut dengan qubit 4 dan 7. Oleh itu, dalam lapisan berkusut tersebut atau sebelum sahaja, ralat Pauli pada mana-mana daripada empat qubit itu boleh menjejaskan pengukuran kemudian. Anda boleh meneruskan penjejakan ke belakang melalui circuit untuk mencari subset gate dan qubit yang berhubung secara sebab-akibat dengan pengukuran. Set sebab-akibat ini membentuk kawasan berbentuk kon dalam ruang (qubit) dan masa (lapisan), yang melahirkan istilah lightcone. Bentuk tepat kawasan itu berbeza dari satu circuit ke circuit yang lain. Oleh sebab analisis ini bergantung pada kesambungan perkakasan dan penempatan gate, ia paling berguna selepas transpilasi, penghalaan dan pengoptimuman susun atur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beyond causal connectivity {#beyond-causal-connectivity}"
msgstr "Melangkaui kesambungan sebab-akibat {#beyond-causal-connectivity}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones extend this idea by also considering which types of errors matter.\n"
msgstr "Shaded lightcones memperluas idea ini dengan turut mempertimbangkan jenis ralat yang penting.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, note the following:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, perhatikan perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Z error immediately before a Z-basis measurement has no effect on the measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr "Ralat Z sejurus sebelum pengukuran asas Z tidak memberi kesan pada hasil pengukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An X error immediately before a Z-basis measurement can dramatically change the result.\n"
msgstr "Ralat X sejurus sebelum pengukuran asas Z boleh mengubah keputusan secara dramatik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some error types therefore deserve more mitigation effort than others. This distinction can substantially reduce the overhead of techniques such as PEC. In practice, the addon generates separate sensitivity analyses for each of the following error types:\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, sesetengah jenis ralat wajar mendapat lebih usaha mitigasi berbanding yang lain. Perbezaan ini boleh mengurangkan overhed bagi teknik seperti PEC dengan ketara. Dalam praktik, addon ini menjana analisis kepekaan yang berasingan bagi setiap jenis ralat berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "X errors\n"
msgstr "X errors\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Z errors\n"
msgstr "Z errors\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Y (or XZ up to a phase) errors\n"
msgstr "Ralat Y (atau XZ sehingga satu fasa)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This error sensitivity generally looks different for each error type, because different causally connected errors have different impacts on the measurement. Note also that the sensitivity changes throughout the circuit. An X error immediately before measurement might be highly damaging, while an error that occurs many layers earlier might have a smaller effect after it propagates through a highly entangled state.\n"
msgstr "Kepekaan ralat ini secara amnya kelihatan berbeza bagi setiap jenis ralat, kerana ralat berhubung sebab-akibat yang berbeza mempunyai kesan yang berbeza pada pengukuran. Perhatikan juga bahawa kepekaan berubah di sepanjang circuit. Ralat X sejurus sebelum pengukuran mungkin sangat merosakkan, manakala ralat yang berlaku beberapa lapisan lebih awal mungkin mempunyai kesan yang lebih kecil selepas merambat melalui keadaan yang sangat terkusut.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Three images showing the same quantum circuit, but with (a) no error, (b) an error just before measurement, and (c) an error earlier in the circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/sensitivity.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Three images showing the same quantum circuit, but with (a) no error, (b) an error just before measurement, and (c) an error earlier in the circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/sensitivity.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones quantify this difference by assigning a sensitivity value to potential errors throughout the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Shaded lightcones mengukur perbezaan ini dengan memberikan nilai kepekaan kepada ralat yang berpotensi di seluruh circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The resulting maps indicate the following:\n"
msgstr "Peta yang terhasil menunjukkan perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where errors matter\n"
msgstr "Di mana ralat penting\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which error types matter\n"
msgstr "Jenis ralat yang mana penting\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How strongly they influence the final observable\n"
msgstr "Sejauh mana kuat ia mempengaruhi observable akhir\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Three images showing heat maps of error sensitivity to three different error types: X, Y, and Z.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/slc-xyz.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Three images showing heat maps of error sensitivity to three different error types: X, Y, and Z.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/slc-xyz.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones do not mitigate errors themselves, but they can help focus mitigation effort where it provides the greatest benefit.\n"
msgstr "Shaded lightcones tidak memitigasi ralat itu sendiri, tetapi ia boleh membantu memfokuskan usaha mitigasi di tempat yang memberikan manfaat terbesar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn and inject noise {#learn-and-inject-noise}"
msgstr "Pelajari dan suntik hingar {#learn-and-inject-noise}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After a circuit has been constructed, optimized, and annotated, two complementary tasks remain: learning the noise, and using the noise model (for example, to inject noise or to propagate the effects of noise).\n"
msgstr "Selepas circuit dibina, dioptimumkan dan dianotasi, dua tugas pelengkap masih tinggal: mempelajari hingar, dan menggunakan model hingar (contohnya, untuk menyuntik hingar atau merambatkan kesan hingar).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 is the current tool for noise learning. The previous NoiseLearner interface accepted entire circuits and produced Pauli-Lindblad noise models. NoiseLearnerV3 instead operates directly on boxed circuit instructions. In summary, NoiseLearnerV3 does the following:\n"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 ialah alat semasa untuk pembelajaran hingar. Antara muka NoiseLearner sebelumnya menerima keseluruhan circuit dan menghasilkan model hingar Pauli-Lindblad. NoiseLearnerV3 sebaliknya beroperasi terus pada arahan circuit yang berkotak. Ringkasnya, NoiseLearnerV3 melakukan perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accepts collections of labeled circuit layers\n"
msgstr "Menerima koleksi lapisan circuit berlabel\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reuses information from repeated layers\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan semula maklumat daripada lapisan yang berulang\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supports measurement-noise learning\n"
msgstr "Menyokong pembelajaran hingar pengukuran\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supports post-processing of learned models\n"
msgstr "Menyokong pasca-pemprosesan model yang dipelajari\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enables noise injection and scaling workflows\n"
msgstr "Membolehkan aliran kerja suntikan dan penskalaan hingar\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This design aligns closely with the layer-oriented workflow of Samplomatic. In particular, NoiseLearnerV3 uses the following methods for each instruction set:\n"
msgstr "Reka bentuk ini selari rapat dengan aliran kerja Samplomatic yang berorientasikan lapisan. Khususnya, NoiseLearnerV3 menggunakan kaedah berikut bagi setiap set arahan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli-Lindblad learning for gate operations\n"
msgstr "Pembelajaran Pauli-Lindblad untuk operasi gate\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX-based learning for measurements\n"
msgstr "Pembelajaran berasaskan TREX untuk pengukuran\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can then use a learned noise model in many of the methods that we have already covered. For example, recall that zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) with gate folding can lead to intractably deep circuits. The alternative method for scaling noise in that case was to sample from a known noise model, which effectively increases the noise level, even by non-integer factors. This method, probabilistic error amplification (PEA), is a good example of how you can use a noise model to mitigate errors. A good noise model is also required for probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and propagated noise absorption (PNA).\n"
msgstr "Anda kemudian boleh menggunakan model hingar yang dipelajari dalam banyak kaedah yang telah kita bincangkan. Sebagai contoh, ingat bahawa ekstrapolasi hingar sifar (ZNE) dengan lipatan gate boleh menghasilkan circuit yang terlalu dalam untuk diurus. Kaedah alternatif untuk menskalakan hingar dalam kes itu ialah mengambil sampel daripada model hingar yang diketahui, yang secara berkesan meningkatkan tahap hingar, malah dengan faktor bukan integer. Kaedah ini, penguatan ralat probabilistik (PEA), ialah contoh yang baik tentang cara anda boleh menggunakan model hingar untuk memitigasi ralat. Model hingar yang baik juga diperlukan untuk pembatalan ralat probabilistik (PEC) dan penyerapan hingar terambat (PNA).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In short, with a high-quality noise model, noise becomes a programmable resource rather than only a source of error.\n"
msgstr "Ringkasnya, dengan model hingar berkualiti tinggi, hingar menjadi sumber yang boleh diprogramkan dan bukan sekadar punca ralat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones versus NoiseLearnerV3 {#shaded-lightcones-versus-noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "Shaded lightcones berbanding NoiseLearnerV3 {#shaded-lightcones-versus-noiselearnerv3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 and SLC are closely related, but they take distinct inputs and answer different questions. SLC determines where to focus mitigation effort. NoiseLearnerV3 characterizes the actual noise present in those regions. These processes also involve different kinds of overhead. The following table summarizes these differences.\n"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 dan SLC berkait rapat, tetapi kedua-duanya mengambil input yang berbeza dan menjawab soalan yang berbeza. SLC menentukan di mana hendak memfokuskan usaha mitigasi. NoiseLearnerV3 mencirikan hingar sebenar yang wujud di kawasan tersebut. Proses ini juga melibatkan jenis overhed yang berbeza. Jadual berikut meringkaskan perbezaan ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|   | Shaded lightcones | NoiseLearnerV3 |\n"
"|---|-------------------|----------------|\n"
"| Purpose | Identifies where mitigation matters | Learns how errors behave |\n"
"| Overhead | Primarily classical overhead | Requires hardware executions |\n"
"| Output | Produces sensitivity maps | Produces noise-channel descriptions |\n"
"| Input | Uses circuit structure and operator propagation | Uses circuit structure and experimental hardware data |\n"
msgstr ""
"|   | Shaded lightcones | NoiseLearnerV3 |\n"
"|---|-------------------|----------------|\n"
"| Tujuan | Mengenal pasti di mana mitigasi penting | Mempelajari bagaimana ralat berkelakuan |\n"
"| Overhed | Terutamanya overhed klasik | Memerlukan pelaksanaan perkakasan |\n"
"| Output | Menghasilkan peta kepekaan | Menghasilkan perihalan saluran hingar |\n"
"| Input | Menggunakan struktur circuit dan perambatan operator | Menggunakan struktur circuit dan data perkakasan eksperimen |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor and runtime execution {#executor-and-runtime-execution}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan Executor dan runtime {#executor-and-runtime-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor performs the final execution step. It can operate on either of the following inputs:\n"
msgstr "Executor melakukan langkah pelaksanaan akhir. Ia boleh beroperasi pada salah satu input berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A template circuit and samplex generated by Samplomatic\n"
msgstr "Circuit templat dan samplex yang dijana oleh Samplomatic\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A conventional quantum circuit without Samplomatic\n"
msgstr "Circuit kuantum lazim tanpa Samplomatic\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this flexibility, you can adopt as many or as few components of the directed execution workflow as you need.\n"
msgstr "Dengan fleksibiliti ini, anda boleh menggunakan seberapa banyak atau sedikit komponen aliran kerja pelaksanaan terarah mengikut keperluan anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor works closely with Samplomatic, which manages randomization choices, shot allocation, noise-injection selections, and related execution metadata, as described previously.\n"
msgstr "Executor berfungsi rapat dengan Samplomatic, yang menguruskan pilihan perawakan, peruntukan shot, pilihan suntikan hingar dan metadata pelaksanaan berkaitan, seperti yang diterangkan sebelum ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For practical examples of the directed execution model, see the [Directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) guide as well as the [tutorials](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/tutorials) and [Qiskit addon documentation](/guides/addons) on [IBM Quantum&reg; Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"
msgstr "Untuk contoh praktikal model pelaksanaan terarah, lihat panduan [Directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) serta [tutorial](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/tutorials) dan [dokumentasi addon Qiskit](/guides/addons) di [IBM Quantum&reg; Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Kesimpulan {#conclusion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modern quantum workflows increasingly rely on a collection of complementary tools rather than a single execution primitive.\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja kuantum moden semakin bergantung pada koleksi alat pelengkap dan bukan satu primitif pelaksanaan tunggal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These tools support every stage of the workflow:\n"
msgstr "Alat ini menyokong setiap peringkat aliran kerja:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Problem mapping\n"
msgstr "Pemetaan masalah\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit construction\n"
msgstr "Pembinaan circuit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation and optimization\n"
msgstr "Transpilasi dan pengoptimuman\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error suppression\n"
msgstr "Penindasan ralat\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error mitigation\n"
msgstr "Mitigasi ralat\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise learning\n"
msgstr "Pembelajaran hingar\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structured execution\n"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan berstruktur\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing\n"
msgstr "Pasca-pemprosesan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Together, tools such as Samplomatic, Executor, NoiseLearnerV3, shaded lightcones, propagated noise absorption, circuit cutting, and AQC-Tensor provide significantly more control than earlier execution models.\n"
msgstr "Bersama-sama, alat seperti Samplomatic, Executor, NoiseLearnerV3, shaded lightcones, penyerapan hingar terambat, pemotongan circuit dan AQC-Tensor memberikan kawalan yang jauh lebih banyak berbanding model pelaksanaan terdahulu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The field continues to evolve rapidly. As quantum processors become larger and more connected, these techniques are likely to play an increasingly important role in achieving useful quantum advantage, and eventually in integrating seamlessly with fault-tolerant quantum computing workflows.\n"
msgstr "Bidang ini terus berkembang pesat. Apabila pemproses kuantum menjadi lebih besar dan lebih bersambung, teknik ini berkemungkinan memainkan peranan yang semakin penting dalam mencapai kelebihan kuantum yang berguna, dan akhirnya berintegrasi dengan lancar bersama aliran kerja pengkomputeran kuantum toleran-kesalahan.\n"
